/*
  ActionItem.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0196 · ActionItem (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/status/ActionItem.tsx) renders NO translated copy of its own: the `title`, `description`,
  and `cta.label` are caller-supplied (already-localized) string props, and the leading glyph + the CTA
  chevron are decorative. The only strings this surface owns are the native a11y additions: the localized
  severity word that names the colour-encoded severity for VoiceOver (the accessible parity of the web's
  colour-only severity signal), and the CTA navigation hints (in-app vs. external) — Apple-HIG affordances
  the web omits but VoiceOver users expect on an actionable affordance.

  All keys live in the per-surface "ActionItem" table and resolve through the P1/S10 facade
  (ActionItemStrings) so the Swift sources hold no hardcoded prose; they fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time. In test / preview bundles
  `NSLocalizedString` returns the value below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Severity words (spoken peer of the web colour-only severity tier) --- */

/* VoiceOver word for the info tier — named so the colour-encoded severity reaches non-sighted users. */
"actionItem.severity.info" = "Information";

/* VoiceOver word for the warn tier. */
"actionItem.severity.warn" = "Warning";

/* VoiceOver word for the error tier. */
"actionItem.severity.error" = "Error";

/* --- CTA VoiceOver hints (shipped native a11y additions; the web omits them) --- */

/* Hint for a CTA that navigates in-app (web internal <Link to>) or fires a handler (web <button>). */
"actionItem.activate.hint" = "Opens details";

/* Hint for a CTA that opens an external target out of the app (web `external` → target="_blank"). */
"actionItem.external.hint" = "Opens in your browser";
